      "sourceHash": "10b7a02f175aba2f7599e57edae6f58b03256b89f68c4d23cef01c4dc335bfad",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.38,
          "end": 3.55,
          "en": "Now, besides to need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.55,
          "end": 5.54,
          "en": "for a web development server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.54,
          "end": 8.876,
          "en": "there also are other reasons for switching to a different,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.876,
          "end": 12.35,
          "en": "to a better development setup,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.35,
          "end": 15.17,
          "en": "because you might not have noticed it yet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.17,
          "end": 19.54,
          "en": "but actually you might want a better developer experience,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.54,
          "end": 23.24,
          "en": "thus far the way we wrote code, it worked,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.24,
          "end": 25.55,
          "en": "but it has certain flaws.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.55,
          "end": 28.19,
          "en": "Our current way of writing and testing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.19,
          "end": 30.59,
          "en": "the Vie App has flaws.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.59,
          "end": 32.85,
          "en": "So let's see what our current state is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.85,
          "end": 36.49,
          "en": "At the moment, we always need to reload the page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.49,
          "end": 39.203,
          "en": "whenever we make any change to our code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.41,
          "end": 42.14,
          "en": "So for example, here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.14,
          "end": 46.6,
          "en": "if I go to my JavaScript file, and let's say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.6,
          "end": 48.913,
          "en": "I do change some data here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.77,
          "end": 52.25,
          "en": "changed the name to Manuel Lorenzo",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.25,
          "end": 53.88,
          "en": "and when I see this on the page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 53.88,
          "end": 57.93,
          "en": "after saving the JavaScript file, I need to reload the page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 57.93,
          "end": 60.42,
          "en": "Now this might not sound like a bad thing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 60.42,
          "end": 63.07,
          "en": "I mean it's really easy and quick to do,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 63.07,
          "end": 67.18,
          "en": "but if you're working on an application on a web application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 67.18,
          "end": 69,
          "en": "for hours and days",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 69,
          "end": 71.05799999999999,
          "en": "and you're writing a lot of code and you wanna test",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 71.05799999999999,
          "end": 72.7,
          "en": "a lot of things,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 72.7,
          "end": 76.31,
          "en": "always having to reload can be very annoying.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 76.31,
          "end": 78.65,
          "en": "It's also worth noting that when you reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 78.65,
          "end": 82.71000000000001,
          "en": "of course you lose all the state of your application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 82.71000000000001,
          "end": 85.75,
          "en": "If this was expanded and you reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 85.75,
          "end": 88.76,
          "en": "you're back to the initial loading state again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 88.76,
          "end": 91.13,
          "en": "and those tiny things can add up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 91.13,
          "end": 94.5,
          "en": "and actually cost you a lot of valuable time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 94.5,
          "end": 98.00999999999999,
          "en": "and make development unnecessary, harder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 98.00999999999999,
          "end": 99.97,
          "en": "or simply take longer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 99.97,
          "end": 102.063,
          "en": "And that's not something you might want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 103.46000000000001,
          "end": 107.86,
          "en": "In addition at the moment in our IDE in our code editor,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 107.86,
          "end": 109.3,
          "en": "Visual Studio Code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 109.3,
          "end": 113.83,
          "en": "the support we get by that tool is highly limited.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 113.83,
          "end": 117.301,
          "en": "For example, the auto-completion is highly limited.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 117.301,
          "end": 120.683,
          "en": "If I, for example, want to call Vue.createApp,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 121.58,
          "end": 123.85,
          "en": "Visual Studio Code doesn't even understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 123.85,
          "end": 126.75,
          "en": "that there is a vue object available.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 126.75,
          "end": 127.94,
          "en": "If I type a dot,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 127.94,
          "end": 131.23,
          "en": "it doesn't know which methods I can call on this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 131.23,
          "end": 134.73,
          "en": "It suggests create app here because I used it before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 134.73,
          "end": 135.79,
          "en": "in that file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 135.79,
          "end": 139.28,
          "en": "but if I didn't, it wouldn't know that it exists.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 139.28,
          "end": 141.38,
          "en": "So that's all the something which is annoying.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 141.38,
          "end": 144.24,
          "en": "It would be nicer to get better IDE support,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 144.24,
          "end": 147.89,
          "en": "to get more IDE auto-completion and for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 147.89,
          "end": 150.22,
          "en": "to also get warnings and errors,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 150.22,
          "end": 151.73,
          "en": "if we add a typo.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 151.73,
          "end": 152.563,
          "en": "At the moment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 152.563,
          "end": 156.47,
          "en": "if I call creatApp like this, because I forgot to E,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 156.47,
          "end": 160.23,
          "en": "yes, the app won't work and we'll get an error here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 160.23,
          "end": 164.07999999999998,
          "en": "in the browser into JavaScript console,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 164.07999999999998,
          "end": 167.29,
          "en": "but we don't get any warning in the editor.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 167.29,
          "end": 170.2,
          "en": "And it would be nice to get a better support here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 170.2,
          "end": 172.44,
          "en": "so that we don't even try to run code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 172.44,
          "end": 174.44299999999998,
          "en": "which has a simple typo will like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 175.8,
          "end": 177.8,
          "en": "Now last but not least thus far,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 177.8,
          "end": 182.72,
          "en": "I always worked with one HTML and one JavaScript file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 182.72,
          "end": 185.56,
          "en": "and we could add more files and combine them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 185.56,
          "end": 189.06,
          "en": "but we would have to manage all those imports",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 189.06,
          "end": 192.53,
          "en": "with script source text, for example, manually.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 192.53,
          "end": 194.57,
          "en": "And from multiple HTML files,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 194.57,
          "end": 196.7,
          "en": "it wouldn't even be that easy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 196.7,
          "end": 199.43,
          "en": "because whilst we could have multiple files,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 199.43,
          "end": 201.21,
          "en": "if we switch between those files,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 201.21,
          "end": 204.01,
          "en": "we would always in the end load a new page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 204.01,
          "end": 206.29,
          "en": "and therefore lose all the states",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 206.29,
          "end": 208.6,
          "en": "that might've been saved in JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 208.6,
          "end": 213.1,
          "en": "So any intermediate results of calculations and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 213.1,
          "end": 216.61,
          "en": "So currently we're kind of limited regarding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 216.61,
          "end": 218.93,
          "en": "how we can split our code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 218.93,
          "end": 221.123,
          "en": "how we can make our code more readable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 222.45,
          "end": 224.36,
          "en": "And of course at the moment having just",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 224.36,
          "end": 226.53,
          "en": "one JavaScript files works,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 226.53,
          "end": 228.48,
          "en": "we don't have that much code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 228.48,
          "end": 231.22,
          "en": "but it's easy to imagine that as we build",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 231.22,
          "end": 233.78,
          "en": "more and more complex applications,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 233.78,
          "end": 235.32,
          "en": "we have more and more code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 235.32,
          "end": 239.12,
          "en": "and we might want to split that code across multiple files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 239.12,
          "end": 242.86,
          "en": "to make every file itself a bit more readable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 242.86,
          "end": 245.77,
          "en": "And for example, things like this template here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 245.77,
          "end": 247.71,
          "en": "which we have for this component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 247.71,
          "end": 250.18,
          "en": "having it in a string like this is a bit annoying,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 250.18,
          "end": 252.51,
          "en": "but at the moment, it's all we can do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 252.51,
          "end": 255.51,
          "en": "We have no better way of defining this template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 255.51,
          "end": 259.81,
          "en": "we can't do it in the HTML file because for components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 259.81,
          "end": 264.433,
          "en": "we can't mount them to HTML as we do with Vue Apps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 266.49,
          "end": 269.12,
          "en": "So that's another thing that would be great",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 269.12,
          "end": 270.89,
          "en": "if we could get rid of it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 270.89,
          "end": 273.36,
          "en": "And therefore, our current state clearly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 273.36,
          "end": 276.46,
          "en": "has some room for improvement.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 276.46,
          "end": 279.2,
          "en": "Our wanted state might look like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 279.2,
          "end": 282.47,
          "en": "It would be great if saved changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 282.47,
          "end": 284.9,
          "en": "So whenever we change something in code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 284.9,
          "end": 288.45,
          "en": "and we saved those changes would be auto-detected,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 288.45,
          "end": 291.22,
          "en": "and then the page would automatically reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 291.22,
          "end": 294.84000000000003,
          "en": "or maybe even better than that, not just reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 294.84000000000003,
          "end": 299.3,
          "en": "but simply update that part of the page that did change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 299.3,
          "end": 302.47,
          "en": "and therefore keep all our state around.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 302.47,
          "end": 305.32,
          "en": "That would be great, it would save us a lot of time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 305.32,
          "end": 306.875,
          "en": "The IDE, so the code editor,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 306.875,
          "end": 310.79,
          "en": "we're using should provide better auto-completion and hints",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 310.79,
          "end": 314.62,
          "en": "to make sure that we're able to find errors quicker",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 314.62,
          "end": 318.23,
          "en": "and avoid writing code that doesn't work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 318.23,
          "end": 321.25,
          "en": "And it would be great if we would have an easy time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 321.25,
          "end": 324.27,
          "en": "splitting our code across multiple files,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 324.27,
          "end": 327.55,
          "en": "defining the templates of components in a nicer way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 327.55,
          "end": 331.09,
          "en": "and using modern JavaScript features like ES modules",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 331.09,
          "end": 333.68,
          "en": "for export and import in JavaScript code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 333.68,
          "end": 335.353,
          "en": "into each other for that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 335.353,
          "end": 338.48,
          "en": "That would be nice and that's our wanted state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 338.48,
          "end": 343.14,
          "en": "And that's exactly where the Vue CLI is able to help us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 343.14,
          "end": 346.09000000000003,
          "en": "So let's find out what exactly the view CLI is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 346.09000000000003,
          "end": 348.08299999999997,
          "en": "how it helps us and how we use it.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
